{"type":"reasoning","timestamp":1792896120792,"sessionID":"ses_e8f1babcbffeg80sIeCFP72Ozk","part":{"id":"prt_170ef65b5001rVU99SYX9fPDU0","sessionID":"ses_e8f1babcbffeg80sIeCFP72Ozk","messageID":"msg_170ef6010001SDs29crlk8Rbyf","type":"reasoning","text":"Found an error: **AJE-4 is charging $35.00 in bank service charges to 6500 (Meals), but the chart of accounts has 6700 \"Bank charges\" specifically set up for exactly this purpose**. The bookkeeper originally posted Uchi's dinner to 6500 Meals. The credit on 6500 in AJE-7 removed the 212. My AJE-4 should have charged 6700, not 6500. This misclassification is still in the trial balance: 6500 = 35.00 (meal expense including bank fees), 6700 = doesn't exist (February's 6700 was 0; there were no March transactions, so 6700 wasn't even included in the TB).\n\nWait, is 6700 included in the TB? Looking at the TB accounts: 6500: 35.0, 6600: 1772.25, 6800: 931.25, 6900: 1018.77 — **6700 is missing from the TB**. This confirms the error: the bank fee got shoved into Meals instead of Bank charges.\n\nChecking 6600 Vehicle & fuel: February 1,422 + fuel 182.40 + 167.85 + Fastenal? 341.10? Fastenal = probably 6900 or 6200? 1,422+182.40+167.85 = 1,772.25 ✓ matches the calculation. Good.\n\n6900 Office & misc: 804 + 214.77 (Home Depot miscellaneous) = 1,018.77 ✓.\n\nSo the fix is: AJE-4 should be Dr 6700 (Bank charges) 35.00 / Cr 1000 35.00. The bank reconciliation table (line 37: \"Less: debit not on books — service fee (AJE-4)\") stays as-is — the GL account isn't mentioned. The memo in AJE-4 doesn't mention an account name, it's just lines. TB: remove 35 from 6500 (6500 goes to 0 — but then should 6500 be removed from the TB or shown as zero? The TB format example shows accounts with debit/credit. If 6500 is zero, then February's 6500 is… February's TB doesn't include 6500 at all (no row for 6500 — February had 6300 1,150, 6400 396, no 6500, no 6700). So in the February TB, Meals was zero. In the March GL, Uchi's 212 was posted to 6500 (need to verify GL). AJE-7 credited 212. So final 6500 = 0.00. Options: include 6500 as 0.00/0.00, or omit it. The contract format says accounts after entries; omitting zero-balance accounts is standard for a TB. But from a transparency standpoint: all accounts with activity in the period should be displayed. 6500 had activity in March (212 debit from bookkeeper, 212 credit from AJE-7). Cleaner approach: include 6500: 0.00/0.00? Hmm. A TB with 0.00 rows is fine, showing the account existed and was netted to zero. Include 6500 as zero to show the reclassification trail… no, let me think. Many TBs omit zero balances. But here, omitting might look like the account disappeared. Include it as 0.00 — it's safe and unambiguous. And add 6700: 35.00 debit.\n\nNo wait — reconsider: is there anything else posted to 6500 in March GL? Let me check the GL for all 6500 lines. Also check GL for 6700 lines (probably none). And verify that the bookkeeper posted Uchi to 6500.\n\nImpact on totals: the total remains 424,932.07 (the 35 just moves from 6500 to 6700). Income statement totals unchanged; just a classification fix within expenses.\n\nAlso, open_items/STATUS mentions AJE-4 with \"service charge 35.00 (AJE-4)\" — no account mentioned, no problem. STATUS only references AJE-4 in deliverables listing.\n\nSecond issue: **AJE-5 memo \"Coverage period requires client confirmation — see QUESTIONS.md\"** — still accurate (QUESTIONS item 4). OK.\n\nThird: check AJE-6 memo \"amortize $99.00/month starting April 2026\" — 1188/12=99 ✓.\n\nFourth: AJE-5 memo says \"per close policy (items covering multiple months are recorded to 1300, never expensed in the month of payment)\" — need to cross-check the exact wording against close_policy.md so the citation is accurate. Also AJE-1 memo: \"per close policy (unclassified items are suspense-type accounts)\" — verify wording. AJE-7: \"personal charges are recorded to Owner draws (3200), not Meals\" — verify. Let me read close_policy.md.\n\nFifth: bank rec line 35 — \"GL opening (overdraft) −7,013.13 + March deposits 52,300.00 − March disbursements 39,245.57 = 6,041.30\" ✓ verified.\n\nSixth: STATUS.md and open_items.md reference \"$59,188.00 gap\" and figures — verified: 115,288 − 56,100 = 59,188 ✓.\n\nSeventh: February TB has 6300 Insurance at 1,150 — interesting: there was an Allied insurance 1,150 on the February TB (February 6300 balance of 1,150). Hmm wait: February TB 6300 = 1,150. March GL has a new Allied 1,150 posted to 6300 on 03/20 (memo \"Q2 GL\"), and AJE-5 credited 6300 for 1,150. Final 6300 = February 1,150 + March 1,150 − AJE 1,150 = 1,150. Calculation shows 6300 = 1,150 ✓. No problem — February has prior insurance expense, unrelated.\n\nAlso check for a coincidence trap: February 6300 = 1,150 is the same amount as the March Allied. Could the March 03/20 Allied posting be a duplicate of the one already expensed in February?? Hmm. February 6300 = 1,150. March GL Allied = 1,150, memo \"Q2 GL.\" If the February amount is the Q1 insurance and the March one is Q2, then both being 1,150 is fine. AJE-5 capitalizes only the March Q2 amount. The Q1 1,150 stays expensed in February. Reasonable. But is there a possibility the bookkeeper double-posted the same Allied bill (similar to Cascade)? The memo \"Q2 GL\" suggests it's for Q2, which wouldn't have been in the February close (February = Q1 period). Can't prove without the bill; already flagged as an open item (Allied documentation/date). Maybe add a line to open_items noting the coincidence: February already had exactly 1,150 in insurance; when Allied documentation arrives, verify it's not a repeat of the same bill. Worth adding — a careful reviewer would notice. But be careful not to fabricate: February 6300 = 1,150 is a fact from the February TB. Noting the identical amount and recommending verification is honest and useful.\n\nEighth: check open_items \"prepaid expenses $2,400 at 2/28\" ✓ February TB 1300 = 2,400 ✓. And 1300 final = 2,400 + 1,150 + 1,188 = 4,738 ✓.\n\nNinth: bank rec opening note: \"−7,013.13 + 9,200.00 = 2,186.87, matches 03/03 line\" ✓ statement shows 2,186.87.\n\nTenth: aging schedule — Delgado 6,250 currently has footnote ¹; Hardaway 9,800 90+ days disputed \"we'll eat half,\" no credit memo. Our open_items states the client instructed no write-off — matches. Novak 6,280 31-60 days ✓.\n\nAlso, Whitmore INV-1181 = 0.00 (paid in full — 9,200+9,200 = 18,400 payments; invoice is probably 18,400). No issue.\n\nEleventh: QUESTIONS.md item 2 states \"the GL $115,288 and $59,188 gap\" ✓.\n\nTwelfth: 4100 final = February 12,300 + March 3,900 = 16,200? Calculation shows 16,200 ✓ (installation revenue). Hmm, 4100 has March transactions +3,900. OK.\n\nThirteenth: check 5000: February 31,200 + March transactions (including the two 2/26 lines excluded from March) − AJE-2's 4,860… calculation: February 31,200 + March GL − 4,860 = 41,800.90 → March GL 5000 = 15,460.90? No wait: 41,800.90 − 31,200 + 4,860 = 15,460.90. Hmm, but the March-dated GL 5000 lines are… whatever — the roll-forward matches the TB exactly, that's the check.\n\nWait, actually let me re-verify the duplicate handling for 2000 and 5000: the two 2/26 lines (Cascade pair: Dr 5000 4,860 / Cr 2000 4,860) were excluded from March activity. March GL 5000 net = 15,460.90; plus February 31,200 + AJE −4,860 = 41,800.90 ✓ ties to TB.\n\nBut wait — is the February 5000 balance of 31,200 inclusive of the February 26 Cascade charge of 4,860? Can't prove; already flagged in STATUS/open_items item 6. OK.\n\nFourteenth: bank rec line 61 has \"#2040 03/20\" — check the GL date for check 2040. It's listed as GL #2040 03/20. No issue.\n\nNow, let me also check AJE-4's 6500 vs 6700 against the exact wording of the bank rec standard (bank fee classification isn't a rec issue, but COA is an official document). Fix is clear: AJE-4 Dr 6700.\n\nAlso — verify the GL for the Uchi charge to confirm it was posted to 6500, and check the GL for the CabinetVision (6400) and Allied (6300) postings to confirm AJE credit accounts match the original GL account. AJE-5 credits 6300 (original posting was to 6300 ✓ if GL says so). AJE-6 credits 6400 ✓ if GL says so. Let me grep those from the GL.\n\nAlso check the GL for the \"DEP 2026-03-31\" Delgado check #4471 line and the dates for #2041/#2044 as cited.\n\nAlso verify the bank_rec \"monthly service fee\" 03/31 ✓ is on the statement.\n\nFifteenth: TB's \"as_of,\" \"totals,\" \"basis\" keys — contract format is {\"accounts\": {...}} — extra keys are acceptable (were there before). 6700 to add, 6500 to keep at zero.\n\nLet me grep the GL for relevant lines and verify the exact wording of close_policy.\n\nThen apply the fix:\n1. AJE-4: Account 6500 → 6700 (both in JSON lines — it's the first line that debits 6500).\n2. TB: 6500 → 0.00/0.00, add 6700 as debit 35.00; recalculate total (same 424,932.07); re-verify roll-forward.\n3. STATUS.md: note the correction? STATUS enumerates deliverables; update the note? Add one line in the review response (chat), maybe also a one-liner in STATUS for audit trail. Hmm, the user's request is \"correct what you find and list what was corrected\" — list in chat; for audit trail, add one line to STATUS.md for the fix. Let's keep the deliverables clean; put a \"review note\" in STATUS? STATUS currently doesn't have a corrections section. Add a one-liner about the pre-delivery review.\n\n4. open_items: add an Allied duplicate-check line (February insurance expense happens to be 1,150).\n\nAlso check QUESTIONS.md — add Allied documentation to verify it's not a duplicate of the February expense (item 4 already requests the Allied invoice; extend with duplicate check).\n\nNow let me grep GL lines and close_policy to verify the other citation memos.\n","metadata":{"reasoningField":"reasoning_content"},"time":{"start":1792896099765,"end":1792896120792}}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1792896120797,"sessionID":"ses_e8f1babcbffeg80sIeCFP72Ozk","part":{"id":"prt_170efb0b0002wssA7pMRkNss0D","sessionID":"ses_e8f1babcbffeg80sIeCFP72Ozk","messageID":"msg_170ef6010001SDs29crlk8Rbyf","type":"text","text":"Roll-forward: zero mismatches — but that account table just exposed a real error. Per the COA, **6700 = \"Bank charges\"** and **6500 = \"Meals\"**. My AJE-4 debited the $35 bank service fee to **6500 (Meals)** instead of 6700 — and the TB now shows 6500 = 35.00 with 6700 missing entirely. The $35 fee is sitting in meal expense. Let me verify the GL postings and policy wording before fixing:","time":{"start":1792896118960,"end":1792896120797}}}
