{"type":"reasoning","timestamp":1792896137676,"sessionID":"ses_e8f1babcbffeg80sIeCFP72Ozk","part":{"id":"prt_170efbd87001kMBKJCqsHOZM3m","sessionID":"ses_e8f1babcbffeg80sIeCFP72Ozk","messageID":"msg_170efb7ef001dGsO5w2leyjMoc","type":"reasoning","text":"Confirming errors:\n- The Uchi dinner was posted to 6500 Meals (GL row 62) — the credit in AJE-7 correctly offsets this.\n- The bank's service charge should belong to 6700 \"Bank fees\" (the COA account for exactly this purpose). My AJE-4 was debiting 6500. Error #1.\n- The GL has no posting for the service charge (confirmed via grep that there's no SERVICE row) ✓, no MOBILE DEPOSIT row ✓.\n- Allied is posted 6300 debit / 2000 credit (GL 36-37) — the credit to 6300 in AJE-5 matches the original posting ✓.\n- CabinetVision is posted to 6400 ✓ AJE-6's credit to 6400 is correct.\n- *4420's XFER: 1000 debit / 4000 credit ✓ AJE-3 is correct.\n\nAlso, the close policy wording I cited in the notes:\n- AJE-1 note: \"anything uncategorized goes to a suspense-type account\" — the actual policy: \"Unidentified receipts are recorded to 2100 'Unidentified receipts / suspense' until identified…not revenue until matched to an invoice or a customer.\" The paraphrase in parentheses is loose but roughly in the spirit… however, the quote-like phrasing \"(anything uncategorized goes to a suspense-type account)\" is presented as the policy's parenthetical description. The policy says \"unidentified receipts,\" not \"anything uncategorized.\" It should be tightened to quote the policy accurately. Similarly, the note in bank_reconciliation lines 86-87: \"the close policy says an uncategorized item goes: suspense liability 2100\" — should say \"unidentified receipts.\" And open_items line 26 onward: \"which is the account your close policy prescribes for anything uncategorized\" — wait, in the rewritten open_items item 1 it says \"the account your close policy prescribes for exactly this\" — that's fine. Let me check the current wording: \"It stays in **suspense liability 2100**, the account your close policy prescribes for exactly this\" — this is fine.\n\nHmm, actually the exact policy is: \"Unidentified receipts are recorded to 2100 ... until identified, and are listed on the open-items note.\" So citing it as a policy for unidentified receipts is accurate. In AJE-1's note, \"(anything uncategorized goes to a suspense-type account)\" misquotes the policy. Fix the wording to: \"per close policy (unidentified receipts go to 2100 'Unidentified receipts / suspense' until identified; not revenue until matched).\"\n\n- AJE-5 note: \"multi-month prepayment per close policy (anything covering more than one month goes to 1300, never the month's expense)\" — policy: \"Prepaid items covering more than one month are capitalized to 1300 and amortized monthly.\" The \"never the month's expense\" part is embellishment; tighten to \"capitalized to 1300 and amortized monthly.\" Fix the wording.\n\n- AJE-6 note: \"12-month prepayment. Move from Software & subscriptions to Prepaid expenses; amortize $99/month beginning April\" — fine, consistent.\n\n- AJE-7 note: \"Close policy: personal charges go to Owner draws (3200), not Meals\" — policy: \"Owner personal transactions through business accounts are recorded to Owner's draws (3200) or Owner's contributions (3100), never to revenue or expense.\" Fix the wording to accurate paraphrase: \"Owner personal transactions through business accounts are recorded to Owner's draws (3200), never to expense.\"\n\n- bank_reconciliation note: \"parked exactly where the close policy says an uncategorized item goes: suspense liability 2100\" → \"where the close policy says unidentified receipts go: 2100 'Unidentified receipts / suspense,' until identified.\"\n\n- AJE-2 note: \"One invoice must be keyed once by invoice number (close policy)\" — policy: \"Vendor bills are recorded once, keyed by vendor invoice number\" ✓ fine.\n\n- bank_rec standard wording: \"an unsupported entry used to force agreement would misstate the records and, for statements furnished to a lender, may be a false statement\" ✓ matches.\n\n- Line 5: \"Form and rules: per AICPA practice aid excerpt (library/bank_rec_standard.md)\" ✓.\n\nSecond error: 6700 is missing from the TB / 6500 is incorrectly 35. Fix:\n- AJE-4 line 1 account 6500→6700. Add a reference to the COA in the note (\"Bank charges (6700) per COA\").\n- TB: 6500 → 0.00/0.00; add 6700 debit 35.00. Total unchanged.\n\nThird issue: Allied duplicate check — the February TB's 6300 = 1,150 is the same amount as March's Allied \"Q2 GL\" 1,150. Possible duplication (like Cascade) — flag in open_items (document request: Allied invoices for both quarters). This is a finding, not a booked change. Worth adding to open_items item 4 and QUESTIONS item 4.\n\nFourth: verify Whitmore INV-1181's zero — the aging schedule shows paid. No problem.\n\nFifth: bank_reconciliation line 37 \"Less: debit not on books — 03/31 monthly service fee −35.00 ... (AJE-4)\" — no mention of account, no problem.\n\nSixth: check the wording on line 23 of the bank rec: \"Check #4471, Delgado, receipt recorded 03/31\" — GL reference \"DEP 2026-03-31\"? The grep didn't show a DEP line for Delgado (the grep searched for \"DEP 2026-03-31\" and didn't match). Let me check the GL deposit lines! Grep for \"Delgado\" and \"Deposit\" in the GL. The bank rec cites 'GL ref DEP 2026-03-31 \"Deposit — Delgado (check #4471)\"'. The grep for \"DEP 2026-03-31\" found nothing — but the GL ref column might be \"DEP\" with date 2026-03-31, and the grep pattern \"DEP 2026-03-31\" spans column boundaries so it wouldn't match as literal text. Need to grep for Delgado instead.\n\nAlso verify DEP lines for Whitmore/Cole/Alvarez for the tie-out table and collections calculation. And payroll lines (Gusto) 7,100/653.20 x2 = total payroll? 6000 Wages final 42,600 = Feb 28,400 + March 14,200 (7,100 x 2)? That means net wages are expensed to 6000 and 6050 = Feb 2,612.80 + 1,306.40 = 3,919.20 ✓ consistent (gross Wages 6000 includes only net wages — this is a note about payroll detail, already flagged).\n\nAlso: 1100 AR — March GL debits to 1100 = invoices 58,420, credits = collections 50,800? February 107,668 + 58,420 − 50,800 = 115,288 ✓ (verified earlier).\n\nAlso: 2300 Sales tax 4,121.55 no change — no March activity; February = March; plausible (no problem, rollforward consistency confirmed; already disclosed in payroll-type verification? Not flagged. Sales tax payable unchanged since Feb despite collections/deposits — worth noting? Sales tax liability stays at 4,121.55 for the whole month; the Gusto TAX ACH 653.20 x2 was posted to 6050 Payroll taxes, not 2300. No remittance of sales tax in March; plausible. Not strictly an error. Leave it; might mention in the payroll/tax detail verification — already flagged as \"payroll detail.\" Sales tax: hmm, the GL posted Gusto tax payments directly to 6050, not 2300 — that's the bookkeeper's method; verification is flagged. Not adding noise.\n\nAlso re-checking STATUS.md content: \"7 entries (AJE-1…AJE-7), each balance-checked and document-referenced\" — AJE-5's document is a GL line + assumption; OK, flagged.\n\nAnd the TB's \"basis\" string — \"The single 2026-02-26 GL row (Cascade CH-7731 email copy)\" — in the earlier summary, we referred to \"two GL rows dated 2026-02-26 (duplicate Cascade CH-7731 pair).\" Need to check the GL for the 2/26 rows: grep lines 1-25. Need to confirm: are the rows one pair (2 rows: 5000 debit + 2000 credit) dated 2026-02-26? The basis says \"The single 2026-02-26 GL row (Cascade CH-7731 email copy) is excluded.\" STATUS says \"Two GL rows ... dated 2026-02-26 (the duplicate Cascade CH-7731 pair).\" If the pair = 2 rows (debit + credit) both dated 2/26, then \"single row\" vs \"two rows\" is inconsistent wording. Check the GL.\n\nAlso verify that the email document (email_owner.txt) has the \"somewhere sensible\" quote and the Pipeline quote — the bank rec's note cites the owner's email. Also check AJE-2's note citation: the \"booked 2/26\" note is in the emailed copy's document — vendor bill documents. Check the documents directory listing: vendor bills. Let me list documents/ and grep email_owner.\n\nAlso check whether there are two copies of Cascade's bill (ch-7731 email + paper) in the documents directory. AJE-2's note: \"Both vendor bill copies in the file set...\" Verify the files exist: grep for files containing 7731.\n\nAlso, the earlier summary claimed \"70 March rows + two 2/26 rows\" — verify: count the rows and their dates.\n\nLet me run these checks.\n\nThe policy citation checks out fine with no issues, but 2 of the parenthetical notes in my AJE memo are misquoting the exact policy language. Also, I need to verify the 2/26 Cascade line, the Delgado DEP line, and the existence of the vendor invoice/email files being cited in the memo:\n","metadata":{"reasoningField":"reasoning_content"},"time":{"start":1792896122247,"end":1792896137676}}}
